1.What is Terraform?
Terraform is an Infrastruture as Code (IaC) tool created by HashiCorp
Instead of manually creating infrastructure from the AWS Console:

Manual Flow:
-----------
AWS Console
|
Create VPC/EC2/S3
|
Create Subnets/EC2 Server/S3 bucket
|
Create SG
|
Launch EC2/S3 bucket etc

we describe the desired infrastruture in code:
----------------------------------------------
resource "aws_instance" "Web" {
  ami   = "AMI_ID"
  instance_type = "t3.micro"
}

Then Terraform create the infrastruture through AWS APIs (Application programming interface)

Terraform configuration
|
Terraform CLI
|
AWS Provider
|
AWS APIs
|
AWS Resources

Note: Terraform can manage AWS, Azure, GCP, Kubernetes, GitHub and many other platforms through providers.

2.What is infrastructure as Code?
Infrastructure as Code Means:
  Infrastructure is defined and managed using "configuration files" instead of manually creating everything.

For example, without Terraform:
-------------------------------
Login AWS
->VPC
->Create VPC
->Create Subnet
->Create Security Group
->EC2
->Launch Instance

With Terraform:
---------------
command : "terraform apply"

Terraform can provision all those resources based on configuration
Advantages:
-----------
.Automation
.Version Control
.Repeatability
.Consistency
.Faster deployment
.Reusable infrastructure
.Reduced manual configuration
.Easier Dev/Test/Prod management
.Infrastucture review through Git
.Diaster recovery/recreation

3.Terraform Terminology:
-------------------------
Provider
A Plugin Terraform uses to communicate with an API/Platform

Example:
provider "aws" {
  region = ap-south-1 / us-east-1
}

Resource
Something Terraform creates/manages.
Exampels:
EC2
VPC
Subnet
Security Group
S3
RDS
IAM
EKS

Example:
resource "aws_vpc" "main" {
  cidr_block = "10.0.0.0/16"
}

Data Source
Reads infromation that already exists

For Example:
data "aws_ami" amazon_linux" {
}

Terraform doesn't create that AMI; it queries AWS for it.

Variable
Input Value:
variable "instance_type" {
  defualt = "t3.micro"
}

Output
Displays useful information after deployment:
output "instance_ip {
  value = aws_instance.web.public_ip
}

state
Terraform keeps track of managed infrastructure using statefile.
Defualt local state: terraform.tfstate

